78e'),(1018,1007,'Test for HDL cholesterol is used along with other lipid tests to determine risk of heart disease.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955c926-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1019,1008,'Test for LDL cholesterol is used along with other lipid tests to determine risk of heart disease.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955c9da-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1020,1009,'Blood component, measure of fat concentration in blood.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955ca8e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1021,1010,'Blood test, composed of cholesterol, HDL, LDL, and triglyceride levels.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955cb38-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1022,1011,'Blood product of muscular cell damage','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955cbec-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1023,1012,'Blood product of anaerobic metabolism','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955cc96-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1024,1013,'The blood test for lipase is used to help diagnose pancreatitis (swelling of the pancreas) and other pancreatic disease. It is also used to a lesser extent in the diagnosis and follow-up of cystic fibrosis, celiac disease, and Crohn\'s disease.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955cd4a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1025,1014,'General indicator of the existence and severity of acute or chronic tissue damage and, sometimes, as a monitor of progressive conditions.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d1dc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1026,1015,'Percent of whole blood that is composed of red blood cells.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d2a4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1027,1016,'Measurement of the amount that red blood cells vary in size','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d362-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1028,1017,'Average concentration of hemoglobin in a given volume of blood.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d420-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1029,1018,'A calculation of the amount of oxygen-carrying hemoglobin inside RBCs. Since macrocytic RBCs are larger than either normal or microcytic RBCs, they would also tend to have higher MCH values.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d4e8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1030,1019,'A broad screening test to check for such disorders as anemia, infection, and many other diseases. Includes white blood cell count, red blood cell count, hemoglobin, hematocrit, indices (MCV, MCH, MCHC, RDW), and often includes platelet count.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d92a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1031,1020,'Immature neutrophils with a crescent shaped nucleus, bands are normal in the circulation in small numbers. If there is a percentage increase of them, there is said to be a left shift. This may happen when an acute infection stimulates increased neutrophils production.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955d9f2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1032,1021,'Agranulocytic leukocyte that normally makes up about 25% of the total white blood cell count but increases in the presence of infection.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955dd1c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1033,1022,'Type of white blood cell which forms an early line of defence against bacterial infections','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955de84-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1034,1023,'Large, circulating, phagocytic white blood cells, having a single well-defined nucleus and very fine granulation in the cytoplasm. Monocytes constitute from 3 to 8 percent of the white blood cells in humans.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955df42-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1035,1024,'A type of white blood cell found in vertebrate blood, containing cytoplasmic granules that are easily stained by eosin or other acid dyes.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955e384-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1036,1025,'Type of leukocyte, with coarse granules that stain blue when exposed to a basic dye. Basophils normally constitute 1% or less of the total white blood cell count but may increase or decrease in certain diseases.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955e44c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1037,1026,'Describes the relative distribution of the different types of white blood cells','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955e780-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1038,1027,'Percentage of T-Suppresor (killer) lymphocytes','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955e8a2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1039,1028,'Count of t-cells which express the CD3 surface receptor','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955ecd0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1040,1029,'Titre level of VDRL test.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955edf2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1041,1030,'Qualitiative test to determine HIV infection','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955f28e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1042,1031,'A treponemal antigen serologic test for syphilis using tanned sheep red blood cells coated with antigen from the Nichol\'s strain of Treponema pallidum and patient serum absorbed with an extract of Reiter treponemes to remove nonspecific antibodies. It is similar in sensitivity and specificity to the FTA-ABS test except that it is less sensitive in detecting primary syphilis.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955f630-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1043,1032,'Qualitative interpretation of TPHA result.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955fa86-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1044,1033,'Test to detect chlamydial infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b955ff2c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1045,1034,'Qualitative test to detect chlamydia infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560558-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1046,1035,'Quantitative measure of Herpes Simplex Virus within a serum sample.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b956081e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1047,1036,'Test to detect neisseria infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b95608e6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1048,1037,'Percentage of HSV sample to a cutoff value.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b956099a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1049,1038,'Qualitative test to detect gonococcal infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560a58-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1050,1039,'Qualitative test to detect trichomonal infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560b16-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1051,1040,'Qualitative interpretation of rapid HIV screening test.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560bd4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1052,1041,'Quantitative result for initial HIV screening test','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560c92-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1053,1042,'Qualitative interpretation of initial screening test for HIV','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560d50-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1054,1043,'Test to detect trichomonal infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560e04-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1055,1044,'Test to detect herpes infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560ec2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1056,1045,'Bands seen on western blot testing for HIV.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9560f76-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1057,1046,'Qualitative test to detect herpes infections via PCR','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9561034-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1058,1047,'Qualitative interpretation of western blot test for HIV confirmation.','en',1,'2004-12-02 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b95610f2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1059,1048,'Question on encounter form: \"Have you disclosed your HIV status to anyone?\"','en',1,'2005-01-06 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b95611b0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1060,1049,'Time range which is less than thirty minutes.','en',1,'2005-01-06 00:00:00',NULL,NULL,'b9561264-8d80-11d8-abbb-00