o continue Category IV treatment. His/her outcome should be reported to the transferring unit so that it can report his/her outcome in the cohort in which s/he originally started Category IV treatment. This group is excluded from the quarterly reports of the receiving unti on registration and treatment result. (Definition from World Health Organization Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant TB)','en',1,'2006-08-23 16:12:20',NULL,NULL,'b9589160-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1558,1530,'Patient that does not fit into any of the following categories - new, relapse, treatment after default, treatment after failure of first treatment, treatment after failure of re-treatment, or transfer in. This group includes Category IV patients who were treated outside DOTS programs and for whom the outcome of the latest treatment is unknown. (Definition from World Health Organization Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant TB)','en',1,'2006-08-23 16:15:16',NULL,NULL,'b9589494-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1559,1531,'Classifies a new MDR-TB patient by previous TB treatment history. Group assignment is determined by history of previous treatment at the time of collection of the sputum sample that was later used to confirm MDR-TB. (Definition from World Health Organization Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant TB)','en',1,'2006-08-23 16:18:41',NULL,NULL,'b958980e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1560,1532,'New smear-positive patients, new smear-negative pulmonary TB with extensive parenchymal involvement, or concomitant HIV disease or severe forms of extrapulmonary TB (Definition from WHO publication, \"Treatment of tuberculosis, Guidelines for National Programs\")','en',1,'2006-08-24 09:36:36',NULL,NULL,'b95898e0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1561,1533,'TB patients that fit one of the following criteria: 1. previously treated sputum smear-positive pulmonary TB including relapse or treatment after default or 2. treatment failure of Category I in settings: a. where representative DRS data show low rates of MDR-TB or individualized drug sensitivity test shows drug-susceptible disease, or b. of poor program performance, absence of representative DRS data or insufficient resouces to implement Category IV treatment. (Definition from WHO publication, \"Treatment of tuberculosis, Guidelines for National Programs\")','en',1,'2006-08-24 09:40:10',NULL,NULL,'b9589b74-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1562,1534,'Chronic (still sputum-positive after supervised re-treatment), and proven or suspected MDR-TB cases (Definition from WHO publication, \"Treatment of tuberculosis, Guidelines for National Programs\")','en',1,'2006-08-24 10:20:40',NULL,NULL,'b9589e26-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1563,1535,'Date on which a patient was registered for MDR-TB treatment.','en',1,'2006-08-24 14:00:36',NULL,NULL,'b9589eee-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1564,1536,'Describes a person that currently has or has had in the past close contact with a person with MDR-TB. This includes members of an MDR-TB patient\'s household and health care workers.','en',1,'2006-08-24 14:26:19',NULL,NULL,'b958a326-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1565,1537,'Describes a person that has been sent to prison','en',1,'2006-08-24 14:27:23',NULL,NULL,'b958a3ee-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1566,1538,'A person that works to provide health care. This includes but is not limited to physicians, nurses, health promoters and DOT workers.','en',1,'2006-08-24 14:29:00',NULL,NULL,'b958a6d2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1567,1539,'Describes a list of factors that increases the patient\'s chances of developing MDR-TB','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:08:09',NULL,NULL,'b958aa4c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1568,1540,'Chronic insufficient excretion of wastes by the kidneys (definition from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-08-24 14:49:21',NULL,NULL,'b958ab78-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1569,1541,'Previous diagnoses that are present. This concept should be used for