0,1551,'Question that asks whether a patient has ever smoked tobacco in the past or smokes currently','en',1,'2006-08-31 14:32:16',NULL,NULL,'b958c3c4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1581,1552,'Question that asks whether the patient has used alcohol in the past or currently uses alcohol.','en',1,'2006-08-31 14:33:19',NULL,NULL,'b958c482-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1582,1553,'Dried blood spot PCR for HIV antigen (in infants)','en',1,'2006-08-31 14:42:54',NULL,NULL,'b958c540-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1583,1554,'Free text field for other medications that a patient has taken in the past.','en',1,'2006-08-31 15:04:53',NULL,NULL,'b958c5f4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1584,1555,'Free text field for other medications that a patient has taken in the past.','en',1,'2006-08-31 15:05:18',NULL,NULL,'b958c6c6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1585,1556,'Free text field for other medications that a patient has taken in the past.','en',1,'2006-08-31 15:05:37',NULL,NULL,'b958c806-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1586,1557,'Free text field for other medications that a patient has taken in the past.','en',1,'2006-08-31 15:05:52',NULL,NULL,'b958c9a0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1587,1558,'Set of concepts describing a patient\'s previous treatment history of non-coded medications','en',1,'2006-08-31 15:07:30',NULL,NULL,'b958cae0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1588,1560,'Question about the patient\'s presenting symptoms for TB','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:49:15',NULL,NULL,'b958cc2a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1589,1561,'Free text field for other, non-coded TB symptoms','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:50:03',NULL,NULL,'b958cd6a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1590,1562,'Patient\'s normal weight in kilograms','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:51:22',NULL,NULL,'b958ceaa-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1591,1563,'Category IV TB patient who has completed treatment according to the program\'s protocol and has at least five consecutive negative cultures from samples collected at least 30 days apart in the final 12 months of treatment. If only one positive culture is reported during that time, and there is no concomitant clinical evidence of deterioration, a patient may still be considered cured, provided that this positive culture is followed by a minimum of three consecutive negative cultures taken at least 30 days apart. (Definition from WHO Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant tuberculosis)','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:56:31',NULL,NULL,'b95914dc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1592,1564,'Category IV patient who has completed treatment according to the program\'s protocol but does not meet the definition for cure because of lack of bacteriological results - i.e. fewer than five cultures were performed in the final 12 months of treatment. (Definition from WHO Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant tuberculosis)','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:58:12',NULL,NULL,'b959166c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1593,1565,'A patient who dies for any reason during the course of MDR-TB treatment. (Definition from WHO )','en',1,'2006-08-31 16:59:01',NULL,NULL,'b95917de-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1594,1566,'Treatment will be considered to have failed if two or more of the five cultures recorded in the final 12 months of therapy are positive, or if any one of the final three cultures is positive. (Definition from WHO Guidelines for the programmatic management of drug-resistant tuberculosis)','en',1,'2006-08-31 17:00:26',NULL,NULL,'b9591928-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1595,1567,'A patient whose treatment was interrupted for two or more consecutive months for any reason. (Definition from WHO)','en',1,'2006-08-31 17:01:55',NULL,NULL,'b9591a86-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1596,1568,'The result of a TB patient\'s treatment course','en',1,'2006-08-31 17:05:20',NULL,NULL,'b9591bda-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1597,1569,'No longer part of a program because they transferred out to another program','en',1,'2006-09-26 16:44:43',NULL,NULL,'b9591d1a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1598,1570,'Reason the patient not on anti-retroviral treatment despite being on active treatment','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:06:48',NULL,NULL,'b9591e5a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1599,1572,'Reason patient is not on ARVs','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:09:42',NULL,NULL,'b9591f9a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1600,1573,'Reason a patient is not on ARVs','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:11:42',NULL,NULL,'b95920d0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1601,1574,'The patient decided not to start treatment','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:12:50',NULL,NULL,'b9592210-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1602,1576,'Status of ARV treatment for patients who seem eligible for treatment','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:18:58',NULL,NULL,'b9592350-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1603,1577,'HIV patient treatment status','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:20:09',NULL,NULL,'b9592486-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1604,1578,'Status of patient apparently eligible for HIV treatment','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:21:00',NULL,NULL,'b95925c6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1605,1579,'HIV treatment stopped','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:22:59',NULL,NULL,'b95926fc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1606,1580,'Why the ARV treatment for the patient has been stopped','fr',1,'2006-08-31 23:28:53',NULL,NULL,'b959283c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1607,1581,'A patient shows side effects of treatment','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:32:07',NULL,NULL,'b959297c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1608,1582,'The reason why ARV treatment was stopped, uncoded','en',1,'2006-08-31 23:36:36',NULL,NULL,'b9592ab2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1609,1583,'Anti-tuberculous drugs that a patient has taken in the past. ','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:01:37',NULL,NULL,'b9592bf2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1610,1584,'The result of a Category IV patient\'s treatment course','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:06:35',NULL,NULL,'b9592d32-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1611,1585,'Patients are considered as cured if his/her smear/culture was positive before the onset of treatment, if they have completed a course of anti-tuberculosis chemotherapy and their smear/culture is negative at 5 or more months of treatment and at the end of treatment.(Definition from WHO)','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:11:24',NULL,NULL,'b9592e72-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1612,1586,'Patients who were smear and culture negative before the onset of treatment and thereafter, and have completed a full course of treatment. Patients who were smear and/or culture positive before the onset of treatment and have completed a full course of anti-tuberculosis chemotherapy but failed to have the required number of negative smears and/or cultures. (Definition from WHO)','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:12:50',NULL,NULL,'b9592fd0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1613,1587,'A patient who failed to achieve bacteriological conversion within 5 (FIVE) months after the start of treatment, or, after previous conversion, becomes sputum smear or culture-positive again. Also a patient who was initially smear-negative before starting treatment and became smear-positive after competing the initial phase of treatment. (Definition from WHO)','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:14:23',NULL,NULL,'b9593142-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1614,1588,'TB regimens with which a patient has been previously treated. ','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:43:01',NULL,NULL,'b95932b4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1615,1589,'Group of concepts associated with the patient\'s previous TB treatment history','en',1,'2006-09-01 10:49:48',NULL,NULL,'b9593444-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1616,1590,'Set of concepts describing a patient\'s previous treatment history with HIV drugs','en',1,'2006-09-01 11:20:49',NULL,NULL,'b9593598-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1617,1591,'Group of concepts that describe the previous treatment history of a TB patient\'s contact or contacts','en',1,'2006-09-01 13:29:13',NULL,NULL,'b95936e2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1618,1592,'Waste material that is secreted by the kidney, is rich in end products (as urea, uric acid, and creatinine) of protein metabolism together with salts and pigments, and forms a clear amber and usually slightly acid fluid (from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:01:56',NULL,NULL,'b95937a0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1619,1593,'Waste matter discharged from the intestines through the anus; excrement (from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:02:36',NULL,NULL,'b9593872-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1620,1594,'The serumlike fluid that circulates through the ventricles of the brain, the cavity of the spinal cord, and the subarachnoid space, functioning in shock absorption (from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:03:19',NULL,NULL,'b959393a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1621,1595,'Source from which a sample was derived for TB culture','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:08:09',NULL,NULL,'b9593a0c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1622,1596,'Free text field for a TB culture source','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:10:10',NULL,NULL,'b9593aca-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1623,1597,'Question that asks whether the patient has a drug-resistant strain of TB. This concept should be used for HIV forms but is not adequate for use on TB forms','en',1,'2006-09-01 14:13:38',NULL,NULL,'b9593b88-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1624,1599,'A malaria diagnosis in the last 12 months','en',1,'2006-09-06 11:05:57',NULL,NULL,'b9593c50-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1625,1600,'A sheet of plastic, sometimes used as a roofing material','en',1,'2006-09-06 13:24:21',NULL,NULL,'b9593d18-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1626,1601,'Question on form.\r\n\r\nPhrased in Kinyarwanda as \"Now that you have improved, can you do the same activity that you used to do? (every day, some days, never)\"','en',1,'2006-09-06 13:32:52',NULL,NULL,'b9593dd6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1627,1604,'Question on a form, asking what secondary activities someone used to do before falling ill.\r\n\r\nPhrased in Kinyarwanda as \"What other activities did you do before you got sick? (for example washing, ironing, shepherding, repairing houses, playing soccer)\"','en',1,'2006-09-06 13:37:41',NULL,NULL,'b9593ea8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1628,1605,'Question asking whether the patient can currently perform activities they used to do before falling ill.\r\n\r\nPhrased in Kinyarwanda as \"Now that you have improved, can you do the same activities that you used to do? (every day, some days, never)\"','en',1,'2006-09-06 13:39:51',NULL,NULL,'b9593f7a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1629,1606,'Mode of transportation','en',1,'2006-09-06 13:48:45',NULL,NULL,'b9594042-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1630,1607,'An opportunistic infection or co-morbid condition that the patient had (either confirmed or presumptive diagnosis) at the time the question was asked','en',1,'2006-09-06 21:56:19',NULL,NULL,'b95940f6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1631,1608,'Construct to hold the details of a patient\'s previous treatment with some medication','en',1,'2006-09-06 16:43:31',NULL,NULL,'b95941b4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1632,1609,'Drug with which the patient had a past course of therapy','en',1,'2006-09-06 16:43:31',NULL,NULL,'b9594510-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1633,1610,'Three-drug cocktail used in treating HIV','en',1,'2006-09-06 16:43:31',NULL,NULL,'b95945c4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1634,1611,'The regimen with which the patient was treated in the past','en',1,'2007-05-13 03:25:44',NULL,NULL,'b9594678-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1635,1612,'Three-drug cocktail used in treating HIV','en',1,'2006-09-06 17:08:19',NULL,NULL,'b959484e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1636,1613,'Three-drug cocktail used in treating HIV','en',1,'2006-09-06 17:10:54',NULL,NULL,'b959490c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1637,1614,'A first-line regimen used for treatment of tuberculosis (in children?)','en',1,'2006-09-06 17:13:10',NULL,NULL,'b95949c0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1638,1615,'A free-text description of a previous treatment with a drug or regimen','en',1,'2006-09-06 18:44:33',NULL,NULL,'b9594b5a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1639,1617,'Free-text comment about previous diagnoses the patient has had.','en',1,'2006-09-06 22:21:13',NULL,NULL,'b9594fb0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1640,1618,'Description of family planning suggested/prescribed to the patient','en',1,'2006-09-06 22:26:21',NULL,NULL,'b959506e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1641,1619,'A generic instruction','en',1,'2006-09-06 22:29:17',NULL,NULL,'b9595118-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1642,1620,'Free-text comments at the end of an examination form.','en',1,'2006-09-06 22:33:06',NULL,NULL,'b95951cc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1643,1621,'Question on form: Has the patient been tested for HIV? ','en',1,'2006-09-08 15:29:03',NULL,NULL,'b9595320-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1644,1622,'Question on form: Has the patient started taking antiretroviral drugs for HIV?','en',1,'2006-09-08 15:30:36',NULL,NULL,'b9595758-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1645,1623,'Question on form: Has the patient started co-trimoxazole preventive therapy?','en',1,'2006-09-08 15:37:33',NULL,NULL,'b959580c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1646,1624,'A test of thyroid stimulating hormone levels that is often the test of choice for evaluating thyroid function and/or symptoms of hyper- or hypothyroidism. ','en',1,'2006-09-11 14:17:57',NULL,NULL,'b95958c0-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1647,1625,'A creatinine clearance test measures how well creatinine is removed from blood by the kidneys. A creatinine clearance test is performed both on a blood sample taken from a vein and on a sample of urine collected over 24 hours (24-hour urine sample). (Definition from health.yahoo.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 14:21:14',NULL,NULL,'b9595bf4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1648,1626,'A bicarbonate (HCO3) test measures the level of bicarbonate in the blood','en',1,'2006-09-11 14:24:57',NULL,NULL,'b9595f1e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1649,1627,'Test in which a sample of urine is prepared in the laboratory and a drop of the urine sediment is put onto a glass slide. The sediment is then examined under a microscope to identify casts, crystals, squamous (flat) cells, and other large objects.','en',1,'2006-09-11 14:57:47',NULL,NULL,'b959604a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1650,1628,'Constipation usually is defined as fewer than three bowel movements per week. Severe constipation is defined as less than one bowel movement per week.  (Definition from www.medinenet.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:22:58',NULL,NULL,'b959641e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1651,1629,'Change in skin color on the spectrum from pink to brownish-black. Usually an unwanted side effect of medication.','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:30:12',NULL,NULL,'b95968d8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1652,1630,'A ringing, swishing, or other type of noise that seems to originate in the ear or head. (Definition from www.medicinenet.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:31:15',NULL,NULL,'b9596c70-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1653,1631,'Tremor is a rhythmic, involuntary muscular contraction characterized by oscillations of a part of the body. (Definition from www.medicinenet.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:32:44',NULL,NULL,'b9597008-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1654,1632,'A harmful or abnormal result to an anti-tuberculous medication. An adverse effect may be caused by administration of a medication or by exposure to a chemical and be indicated by an untoward result such as by illness or death.','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:34:31',NULL,NULL,'b959747c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1655,1633,'A thiosaemicarbazone that is used in association with other antimycobacterial agents in the initial and continuation phases of antituberculosis regimens','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:42:29',NULL,NULL,'b9597936-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1656,1634,'Terizidone is a combination of two cycloserine molecules. It is an anti-tuberculous drug used in treating multidrug-resistant TB.  TERIZIDONE is considered effective in the treatment of TB and may also be useful for the treatment of urinary tract infections including those due to TB. It is recommended for the treatment of MDR-TB patients in both the intensive and continuation phases. Oral bacteriostatic second-line TB med.','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:46:45',NULL,NULL,'b959814c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1657,1635,'Adverse event in which no intervention was required','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:50:08',NULL,NULL,'b9598232-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1658,1636,'Adverse event which required palliative intervention (e.g. pain killer)','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:50:50',NULL,NULL,'b95982fa-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1659,1637,'Adverse event requiring a change in treatment. Should be referred to an MDR center','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:51:55',NULL,NULL,'b95983b8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1660,1638,'Grades the severity of an adverse event on a three-point scale','en',1,'2006-09-11 15:52:50',NULL,NULL,'b9598480-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1661,1639,'Restoration or return to health from sickness (Definition from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:21:39',NULL,NULL,'b959853e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1662,1640,'The total and permanent cessation of all the vital functions of an organism (Definition from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:29:42',NULL,NULL,'b95985fc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1663,1641,'Describes the outcome of an intervention for a patient\'s adverse reaction to a medication','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:32:19',NULL,NULL,'b95986ba-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1664,1642,'Drug is no longer given to a patient','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:33:22',NULL,NULL,'b9598778-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1665,1643,'Free text field for other non-coded action taken in response to a patient\'s adverse reaction to a medication','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:36:26',NULL,NULL,'b9598836-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1666,1644,'The elimination or reduction of natural or acquired reactivity or sensitivity to an external stimulus, as an allergen (Definition from Dictionary.com)','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:40:27',NULL,NULL,'b95988f4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1667,1645,'Describes the action taken to a patient\'s adverse reaction to a medication','en',1,'2006-09-11 16:41:51',NULL,NULL,'b95989c6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1668,1646,'A list of TB medications that could be responsible for a patient\'s adverse effect','en',1,'2006-09-12 09:09:09',NULL,NULL,'b9598a84-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1669,1647,'The program where drugs prevent the maternal to child transmission of HIV during pregnancy','en',1,'2006-09-18 08:59:47',NULL,NULL,'b9598b42-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1670,1648,'The program for tracking TB','en',1,'2006-09-18 09:00:46',NULL,NULL,'b9598c00-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1671,1649,'Voluntary Counseling and Testing Program for HIV','en',1,'2006-09-18 09:03:42',NULL,NULL,'b9598cbe-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1672,1649,'conseil et dépistage volontaires du VIH','fr',1,'2007-10-12 10:32:01',NULL,NULL,'b9598d7c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1673,1650,'This keeps track of how we first admitted the patient ? i.e. through VCT, PMTCT, Primary Care, TB program, etc.  This can be different from how a patient was enrolled in a particular program ? for example, we could enroll a patient for the first time through Primary Care, realize he has TB, and then later enroll him in the HIV/ARV program because we discovered it in the TB program.','en',1,'2007-04-30 21:45:57',NULL,NULL,'b9598e3a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1674,1651,'A mode of admission','en',1,'2006-09-18 09:28:17',NULL,NULL,'b9598f20-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1675,1652,'Set of concepts describing a patient\'s adverse effect to TB medications','en',1,'2006-09-20 15:02:31',NULL,NULL,'b9598fde-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1676,1653,'Question from intake form:  \"Does your house have windows?\".  ]This doesn\'t mean the ones from Microsoft.','en',1,'2006-09-21 11:53:15',NULL,NULL,'b959909c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(1677,1654,'Question on the intake form:  \"number of pigs that the patient\'s family owns?\"\r\n','en',1,'2006-09-21 11:54:45',NULL,NULL,'b959915a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(167