mally fast breathing. A respiratory rate that is too rapid. The normal rate of respirations (breaths per minute) depends on a number of factors, including the age of the individual and the degree of exertion.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:09:00',NULL,NULL,'b96624e2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3969,3232,'This is when a patient uses additional muscles in addition to the intercostals and diaphram to inhale or exhale. An example is that some people will raise their shoulders in order to increase the volume of the chest, increasing the tidal volume of each breath.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:14:19',NULL,NULL,'b96625b4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3970,3233,'General Exam Finding other than those provided. Open Text. ','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:17:18',NULL,NULL,'b9662686-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3971,3234,'Pink eye is the most obvious symptom of conjunctivitis, which involves inflammation of the clear membrane covering the white part of the eye and interior lining of the eyelids. Pink eye can refer to all types of conjunctivitis, or just to its contagious forms.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:25:04',NULL,NULL,'b9662744-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3972,3235,'The jugular venous pressure (JVP, sometimes referred to as jugular venous pulse) is the indirectly observed pressure over the venous system. It can be useful in the differentiation of different forms of heart and lung disease.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:29:19',NULL,NULL,'b9662816-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3973,3236,'State of lung clarity','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:35:15',NULL,NULL,'b96628de-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3974,3237,'General findings while examining the lungs.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:35:48',NULL,NULL,'b966299c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3975,3238,'Findings noted on examination of the lungs.','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:36:49',NULL,NULL,'b9662a50-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3976,3239,'Rales, crackles or crepitations, are the clicking, rattling, or crackling noises heard on auscultation of (listening to) the lung with a stethoscope during inhalation','en',1,'2008-06-18 11:39:12',NULL,NULL,'b9662b0e-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3977,3240,'Region of lung where abnormality is observed by clinician.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:04:38',NULL,NULL,'b9662bd6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3978,3241,'The absence of cardiac murmurs','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:09:20',NULL,NULL,'b9662f28-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3979,3242,'A heart rate over 100 beats a minute is called tachycardia. Some tachycardias are relatively harmless and need no treatment, but others can be life-threatening.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:11:47',NULL,NULL,'b9662fe6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3980,3243,'Soft abdomen observed during current encounter.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:16:55',NULL,NULL,'b96630b8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3981,3244,'The absence of abdominal tenderness when examining a patient','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:18:49',NULL,NULL,'b9663176-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3982,3245,'No enlargement of the spleen.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:22:45',NULL,NULL,'b9663234-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3983,3246,'No enlargement of the liver. ','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:24:31',NULL,NULL,'b96632e8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3984,3247,'No abnormal accumulation of serous fluid in the abdominal cavity.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:25:38',NULL,NULL,'b96633a6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3985,3248,'Undergoing pulsation; vibrating organ','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:40:04',NULL,NULL,'b966345a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3986,3249,'A general measure of an observation during an encounter.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:42:49',NULL,NULL,'b9663518-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3987,3250,'A general measure of an observation during an encounter.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:46:12',NULL,NULL,'b96635d6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3988,3251,'Anatomic location in the right lower quadrant of the abdomen.','en',1,'2008-06-18 13:50:57',NULL,NULL,'b966368a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(3989,3252,'Anatomic location in the left upper quadrant of the abdomen.','en',1,'200