ly contains it.','en',1,'2010-02-18 13:20:37',NULL,NULL,'b9773ce6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5773,6947,'A hernia present at the site of the umbilicus (commonly called a navel, or belly button).','en',1,'2010-02-18 13:22:08',NULL,NULL,'b9773e08-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5774,6948,'A viral inflammation of the larynx.','en',1,'2010-02-18 13:26:33',NULL,NULL,'b9773f2a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5775,6949,'An autosomal recessive genetic disorder of DNA repair in which the ability to repair damage caused by ultraviolet (UV) light is deficient.','en',1,'2010-02-18 13:28:09',NULL,NULL,'b977404c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5776,6950,'A first-generation cephalosporin antibiotic.  It is an orally administered agent with a similar antimicrobial spectrum to the intravenous agents cefalotin and cefazolin. It is commonly marketed under the trade name Keflex (Lilly), Sporidex (Ranbaxy) or Nufex.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:24:49',NULL,NULL,'b9774178-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5777,6951,'A nitrate used pharmacologically as a vasodilator, e.g. in angina pectoris but also for anal fissure, a condition which is known to involve decreased blood supply leading to poor healing. It is also used as a direct vasodilator to treat congestive heart failure.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:31:11',NULL,NULL,'b97742ae-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5778,6952,'Part of the artemisinin group of drugs that treat malaria. It is a semi-synthetic derivative of artemisinin that is water-soluble and may therefore be given by injection.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:39:35',NULL,NULL,'b97743ee-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5779,6953,'A drug combindation used to treat malaria.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:40:26',NULL,NULL,'b977451a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5780,6954,'Amphotericin B (Fungilin, Fungizone, Abelcet, AmBisome, Fungisome, Amphocil, Amphotec) is a polyene antifungal drug, often used intravenously for systemic fungal infections.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:44:14',NULL,NULL,'b977463c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5781,6955,'A medicinal drug used in the treatment of Human African trypanosomiasis. It is also sold under the trade names Mel B and Melarsen Oxide-BAL.  Melarsoprol is also used in the treatment of Chagas disease and sleeping sickness, the former caused by Trypanosoma cruzi and the latter by Trypanosoma brucei.','en',1,'2010-02-18 14:56:33',NULL,NULL,'b9774772-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5782,6956,'Drug used for treatment of human sleeping sickness caused by trypanosomes and helminthiasis.  It has been used in the treatment of onchocerciasis.  It has been investigated as treatment for prostate cancer.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:05:19',NULL,NULL,'b97748a8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5783,6957,'A biological product used in the treatment of venomous bites or stings. ','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:09:55',NULL,NULL,'b97749f2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5784,6958,'Any organic compound in which a hydroxyl functional group (-OH) is bound to a carbon atom, usually connected to other carbon or hydrogen atoms.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:34:36',NULL,NULL,'b9774bdc-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5785,6959,'Salicylic acid is a beta hydroxy acid it is best known for its use in anti-acne treatments.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:39:26',NULL,NULL,'b9774e70-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5786,6960,'A constituent of Whitfield\'s Ointment which is used for the treatment of fungal skin diseases such as tinea, ringworm, and athlete\'s foot.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:40:42',NULL,NULL,'b977505a-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5787,6961,'Commonly known as Whitfield\'s Ointment, used for the treatment of fungal skin diseases such as tinea, ringworm, and athlete\'s foot.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:41:20',NULL,NULL,'b977526c-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5788,6962,'The active ingredient in Devrom (internal deodorant), an over-the-counter FDA-approved medicine commonly used to treat malodor by deodorizing flatulence and stool. Also, it has been used to treat Helicobacter pylori infection and is used in wound therapy. As an internal deodorant, it is commonly used by individuals who have had ostomy surgery, bariatric surgery, fecal incontinence, and irritable bowel syndrome.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:44:11',NULL,NULL,'b9775474-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5789,6963,'A chemical antiseptic. It kills (is bactericidal to) both gram-positive and gram-negative microbes, although it is less effective with some gram-negative microbes. It is also bacteriostatic.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:49:00',NULL,NULL,'b97756a4-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5790,6964,'A fluorophore commonly used as a diagnostic tool in the field of ophthalmology and optometry, where topical fluorescein is used in the diagnosis of corneal abrasions, corneal ulcers and herpetic corneal infections. It is also used in rigid gas permeable contact lens fitting to evaluate the tear layer under the lens.\r\n\r\nIntravenous or oral fluorescein is used in fluorescein angiography in research and to diagnose and categorize vascular disorders in e.g. legs, including retinal disease macular degeneration, diabetic retinopathy, inflammatory intraocular conditions, and intraocular tumors , and increasingly during surgery for brain tumors.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:53:39',NULL,NULL,'b97758b6-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5791,6965,'An organic compound, that is a colorless, odorless, viscous liquid widely used in pharmaceutical formulations.','en',1,'2010-02-18 15:56:15',NULL,NULL,'b9775afa-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5792,6966,'Chemical element, a member of the halogens.','en',1,'2010-02-18 16:01:05',NULL,NULL,'b9775cf8-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5793,6967,'The chemical element that has the atomic number 16. It is denoted with the symbol S.','en',1,'2010-02-18 16:08:12',NULL,NULL,'b9775ee2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5794,6968,'Chemical compounds.','en',1,'2010-02-18 16:09:33',NULL,NULL,'b97760c2-8d80-11d8-abbb-0024217bb78e'),(5795,6969,'Refer the patient to an ART clinician?','en',1,'2010-02-23 08:52:28',NULL,NULL,'b97